# CMZ, showing a credential with two attributes, both hidden: one
# commitment equation per attribute, then the validity equation that
# ties the commitments to a credential the issuer signed.
# Examples/Cmz.v, show_stmt, at k = 2.
#
# Attribute a_i is committed under the rerandomised MAC point P and
# blinded by z_i under A; the validity equation recomputes V from the
# blinding factors under the issuer's per-attribute keys X_i.
secrets a0 z0 a1 z1 zQ
claims  a0 z0 a1 z1 zQ
eq  C0   P   A   1   1   1
eq  C1   1   1   P   A   1
eq  V    1   X0  1   X1  B

# An instance: one distinct generator per base name, so the
# environment is faithful and the verdict above transfers to it.
# The exponents are ours and carry no meaning; every element of a
# prime-order group is a generator power, so this is simply a way
# to write distinct elements down.
point P   2
point A   3
point X0  5
point X1  7
point B   11
